{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 310,
    "dDurationMs": 3830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Did you know that if the sun were fueled by\ncombustion of, say, gasoline or wood, it would"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4140,
    "dDurationMs": 1750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "burn out in just a few millennia?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5890,
    "dDurationMs": 3020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So how is it still here after 4.5 billion\nyears?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8910,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Physics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9910,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The sun is like a big nuclear submarine…\nin the sky."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13060,
    "dDurationMs": 4660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's right - it's fueled by nuclear reactions\nthat fuse hydrogen atoms together into helium"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17720,
    "dDurationMs": 4030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and other heavier elements, releasing huge\namounts of energy in the process."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21750,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this way the sun is slowly converting its\nmass into energy – in the form of sunlight!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25560,
    "dDurationMs": 3039,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it has more than enough fuel to last billions\nof years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28599,
    "dDurationMs": 4921,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But nuclear fusion's no walk in the park - on\nearth we need to heat hydrogen up 100x hotter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33520,
    "dDurationMs": 1340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than the sun to get a fusion reaction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34860,
    "dDurationMs": 2660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So how does the sun do it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37520,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Quantum tunneling."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38520,
    "dDurationMs": 3850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's a small chance (which I'll explain\nlater) that hydrogen atoms, even if they aren't"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42370,
    "dDurationMs": 2431,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "quite hot enough for fusion, will fuse together\nanyway."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44801,
    "dDurationMs": 5229,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the sun is SO big and has so much hydrogen\nthat these small chances happen all the time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50030,
    "dDurationMs": 1730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that's what keeps the sun energized!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51760,
    "dDurationMs": 11510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So when the sun shines tomorrow, give thanks\nto quantum mechanics."
    } ]
  } ]
}
